1
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,440
The tide's against us.

2
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:32,930
Aye, but we have the wind.

3
00:03:32,930 --> 00:03:34,940
She'll blow us straight to the gate.

4
00:03:35,810 --> 00:03:36,990
You're coming home.

5
00:03:36,990 --> 00:03:39,340
King's Landing hasn't been home for 20 years.

6
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:45,330
I spent most of my life dodging the Royal Fleet.

7
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:49,530
And now I'm sailing right at them.

8
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:51,880
This is the Royal Fleet.

9
00:03:52,090 --> 00:03:54,020
And you're not a smuggler anymore, you're the High Captain.

10
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:57,150
Of course there are several Royal Fleets at the moment.

11
00:03:57,150 --> 00:03:59,780
Not after tonight. When the sun rises,

12
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:01,710
Stannis will sit on the Iron Throne

13
00:04:01,970 --> 00:04:03,410
and you will be his Hand.

14
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:05,160
- Gods be good. - God.

15
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:07,750
Father, there is only one and he watches over us.

16
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:09,700
- But not over them? - Over all of us.

17
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:12,600
The people of King's Landing did not choose the false king

18
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:14,180
Joffrey Baratheon.

19
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:16,660
They will be glad to see his head on a spike.

20
00:04:16,660 --> 00:04:18,890
Well, first we have to put it there.

21
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,680
Our ships outnumber theirs 10 to one.

22
00:04:22,030 --> 00:04:24,050
Our army outnumber theirs five to one.

23
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:26,400
Those walls have never been breached.

24
00:04:26,830 --> 00:04:28,420
And the men guarding the walls,

25
00:04:28,430 --> 00:04:31,000
when they see you, they don't see a liberator.

26
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:34,920
They see a stranger come to set their city on fire.

27
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:37,330
I have faith in the Lord of Light.

28
00:04:37,430 --> 00:04:39,260
I have faith in our cause.

29
00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:42,690
And I have faith in my Captain.

30
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:19,090
Are you afraid, my lion?

31
00:05:23,870 --> 00:05:28,570
If the city falls, Stannis will burn every Lannister he can find.

32
00:05:30,410 --> 00:05:32,040
Of course I'm afraid.

33
00:05:35,330 --> 00:05:37,170
I won't let them hurt you.

34
00:05:41,970 --> 00:05:43,490
I'm a Lannister.

35
00:05:43,970 --> 00:05:46,240
I don't have a choice in all this.

36
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,610
But it's not your war.

37
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:57,640
It is now.

38
00:06:02,770 --> 00:06:05,120
You can't fuck your way out of everything.

39
00:06:06,550 --> 00:06:08,340
I have so far.

40
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:14,440
Do you remember what you said when you met me in your tent?

41
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:17,840
That I should make love to you

42
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:20,000
like it was your last day on this earth.

43
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,870
As you know, Your Grace,

44
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:37,830
it is not only the sworn duty of a Maester

45
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:41,160
to carry out the wishes of the house he serves,

46
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:47,210
but also to offer guidance and counsel in times of war.

47
00:06:47,210 --> 00:06:49,650
Your words are always wise and measured.

48
00:06:49,650 --> 00:06:51,440
- If you could... - If anything,

49
00:06:52,110 --> 00:06:56,280
a Maester's duties become more urgent

50
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:59,920
in times of war and turmoil.

51
00:07:00,790 --> 00:07:04,010
I remember back in the days of king...

52
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:05,650
You brought me something?

53
00:07:06,850 --> 00:07:08,000
Yes.

54
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:13,850
Essence of Nightshade

55
00:07:14,010 --> 00:07:17,880
is as dangerous as it is efficacious.

56
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:20,960
A single drop in a cup of wine

57
00:07:21,430 --> 00:07:25,260
suffices to soothe ragged nerves.

58
00:07:25,310 --> 00:07:30,140
Three drops will bring on a deep and dreamless sleep.

59
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:33,020
10 drops, however--

60
00:07:33,030 --> 00:07:34,760
I know what 10 drops will bring.

61
00:07:34,780 --> 00:07:38,810
- Your Grace, if I may ask-- - You may not.

62
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:42,850
You must have a lot of work to do.

63
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:46,060
I'm sure many brave men will need your wisdom soon.

64
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:50,670
Yes. A siege is very...

65
00:07:50,670 --> 00:07:53,190
Be careful on the stairs, Grand Maester. There are so many.

66
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:57,780
Your Grace.

67
00:08:01,170 --> 00:08:03,550
*And so he spoke,*

68
00:08:03,550 --> 00:08:08,450
*that Lord of Castamere,*

69
00:08:08,450 --> 00:08:13,440
*But now the rains weep o'er his hall,*

70
00:08:13,440 --> 00:08:18,040
*with no one there to hear.*

71
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:22,560
*Yes, now the rains weep o'er his hall,*

72
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:28,960
*and not a soul to hear.*

73
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:32,480
- To the boys! - Lannisters!

74
00:08:32,690 --> 00:08:34,770
Where'd you learn the Lannister song?

75
00:08:34,770 --> 00:08:36,170
Drunk Lannisters.

76
00:08:38,470 --> 00:08:40,270
You've got a pretty voice.

77
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:41,720
Thank you very much.

78
00:08:42,210 --> 00:08:43,990
And I like your nose.

79
00:08:44,550 --> 00:08:46,530
How many times you break it?

80
00:08:48,930 --> 00:08:50,360
Well, now let's see.

81
00:08:50,870 --> 00:08:53,560
First time I was five.

82
00:08:53,980 --> 00:08:56,000
Me mom smacked me with an iron poker.

83
00:08:57,150 --> 00:08:59,000
Oh, it wasn't me she was aiming at.

84
00:08:59,630 --> 00:09:01,370
She was trying for me little brother.

85
00:09:01,630 --> 00:09:03,250
Now he was a real pest.

86
00:09:03,250 --> 00:09:06,650
Second time I was nine.

87
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:09,910
Got in a scrap with a few older boys.

88
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:11,760
They won.

89
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:14,460
Third time...

90
00:09:21,670 --> 00:09:24,350
Eh, you don't want to know about the third time.

91
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:30,080
Poor nose.

92
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:32,050
Don't feel sorry for him.

93
00:09:32,110 --> 00:09:34,550
He'll be halfway up your ass before the night's through.

94
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:47,820
Welcome, friends.

95
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:53,730
This round's on me.

96
00:10:03,310 --> 00:10:04,990
I don't think he likes me.

97
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:20,470
You think you're a hard man?

98
00:10:22,110 --> 00:10:23,700
I know it.

99
00:10:28,850 --> 00:10:30,330
It's warm in here.

100
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:33,040
We've got beautiful women

101
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:34,750
And good brown ale.

102
00:10:35,110 --> 00:10:36,720
Plenty for everyone.

103
00:10:37,850 --> 00:10:39,340
And all you want

104
00:10:39,340 --> 00:10:42,360
is to put one of us in the cold ground

105
00:10:42,630 --> 00:10:44,860
with no women to keep us company.

106
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:47,010
Oh, there's women in the ground.

107
00:10:47,270 --> 00:10:49,270
I put some there myself.

108
00:10:49,970 --> 00:10:51,470
So have you.

109
00:10:53,290 --> 00:10:55,600
You like fucking and drinking

110
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,180
and singing.

111
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:00,960
But killing...

112
00:11:02,090 --> 00:11:03,920
Killing's the thing you love.

113
00:11:05,580 --> 00:11:07,240
You're just like me.

114
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:12,480
Only smaller.

115
00:11:15,090 --> 00:11:16,510
And quicker.

116
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:23,200
Your Lord Imp is gonna miss you.

117
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:30,910
Aye.

118
00:11:34,090 --> 00:11:36,290
I expect he will someday.

119
00:11:42,020 --> 00:11:43,170
Here we are.

120
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:57,130
One more drink before the war?

121
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:58,590
Shall we?

122
00:12:10,180 --> 00:12:12,500
I've always hated the bells.

123
00:12:12,550 --> 00:12:14,140
They ring for horror...

124
00:12:14,370 --> 00:12:17,180
A dead king, a city under siege.

125
00:12:17,180 --> 00:12:19,120
- A wedding. - Exactly.

126
00:12:21,390 --> 00:12:23,280
Podrick, is that it?

127
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:25,880
"Is that it?" nice touch.

128
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:28,800
As if you don't know the name of every boy in town.

129
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:31,990
I'm not entirely sure what you're suggesting.

130
00:12:31,990 --> 00:12:35,140
I'm entirely sure you're entirely sure what I'm suggesting.

131
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,510
Do you trust him?

132
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:42,970
Oddly enough, I do.

133
00:12:44,490 --> 00:12:45,560
Good.

134
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,710
The map you asked for.

135
00:12:57,970 --> 00:13:00,490
There must be 20 miles of tunnels beneath the city.

136
00:13:00,490 --> 00:13:02,140
Closer to 50.

137
00:13:02,260 --> 00:13:05,700
The Targaryens built this city to withstand a siege

138
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:09,630
and to provide escape if necessary.

139
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:11,090
I'm not escaping.

140
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,760
Strange as it sounds, I'm the captain of the ship.

141
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,470
And if the ship goes down, I go with her.

142
00:13:15,470 --> 00:13:17,180
That is good to hear.

143
00:13:17,190 --> 00:13:21,600
Though I'm sure many captains say the same while their ship is afloat.

144
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:25,530
You look well suited for battle, My Lord.

145
00:13:25,530 --> 00:13:27,010
Well, I'm not.

146
00:13:27,430 --> 00:13:29,940
For all our sakes, I hope you are wrong.

147
00:13:31,330 --> 00:13:34,130
My little birds tell me that Stannis Baratheon

148
00:13:34,130 --> 00:13:37,450
has taken up with a red priestess from Asshai.

149
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:38,920
What of it?

150
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:42,040
You don't believe in the old powers, My Lord?

151
00:13:42,390 --> 00:13:45,960
Blood spells, curses, shape-shifting... what do you think?

152
00:13:46,590 --> 00:13:53,070
I think you believe in what you see and in what those you trust have seen.

153
00:13:54,530 --> 00:13:57,450
You probably don't entirely trust me.

154
00:13:57,510 --> 00:13:59,330
Mm, don't take it personally.

155
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:01,550
I don't entirely trust myself.

156
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,860
And yet I have seen things

157
00:14:04,590 --> 00:14:06,210
and heard things...

158
00:14:06,630 --> 00:14:10,900
Things you have not, things I wish I had not.

159
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:16,920
I don't believe I've ever told you how I was cut.

160
00:14:18,930 --> 00:14:20,600
No, I don't believe you have.

161
00:14:22,470 --> 00:14:24,980
One day I will.

162
00:14:26,340 --> 00:14:30,250
The dark arts have provided Lord Stannis with his armies

163
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:32,880
and paved his path to our door.

164
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:37,530
For a man in service to such powers to sit on the Iron Throne,

165
00:14:37,780 --> 00:14:40,090
I can think of nothing worse.

166
00:14:41,070 --> 00:14:42,640
And tonight,

167
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:46,790
I believe you are the only man who can stop him.

168
00:15:13,570 --> 00:15:15,230
They're welcoming the new king.

169
00:15:15,710 --> 00:15:18,170
I've never known bells to mean surrender.

170
00:15:19,610 --> 00:15:21,670
They want to play music with us? Let's play.

171
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:24,940
- Drums. - Drums!

172
00:15:50,170 --> 00:15:53,060
- Remember, wait till... - The ships are in the bay.

173
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:54,500
They must be far enough in so they won't be...

174
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:56,330
I know what "in" means.

175
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,950
- Do you know how to use that? - I chopped wood once.

176
00:15:58,950 --> 00:16:01,090
No, I watched my brother chopping wood.

177
00:16:01,090 --> 00:16:03,020
I saw you kill a man with a shield.

178
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:04,840
You'll be unstoppable with an axe.

179
00:16:06,490 --> 00:16:08,620
- Don't get killed. - Nor you, my friend.

180
00:16:08,660 --> 00:16:11,960
- Oh, are we friends now? - Of course we are.

181
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:15,400
Just because I pay you for your services doesn't diminish our friendship.

182
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:16,990
Enhances it, really.

183
00:16:16,990 --> 00:16:19,670
Oh, enhances. Fancy word for a sellsword.

184
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:21,760
Been spending time with fancy folks.

185
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:36,530
Lady Sansa and, uh, Sheila.

186
00:16:37,410 --> 00:16:38,230
Shae.

187
00:16:38,230 --> 00:16:39,770
Shae, yes.

188
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,600
Surely my sister has asked you to join

189
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,930
the other highborn ladies in Maegor's Holdfast.

190
00:16:43,930 --> 00:16:47,460
She has, my lord, but King Joffrey sent for me to see him off.

191
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:49,790
Sansa.

192
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:51,850
He's been a great romantic, my nephew.

193
00:16:51,850 --> 00:16:53,430
Sansa, come here.

194
00:16:56,010 --> 00:16:58,190
I will pray for your safe return, My Lord.

195
00:16:59,130 --> 00:17:00,090
Will you?

196
00:17:00,090 --> 00:17:02,200
Just as I pray for the king's.

197
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:08,350
Stay safe, My Lady.

198
00:17:08,350 --> 00:17:09,780
And you, my lion.

199
00:17:15,690 --> 00:17:17,870
Your king rides forth to battle.

200
00:17:18,750 --> 00:17:20,810
You should see him off with a kiss.

201
00:17:22,020 --> 00:17:23,490
My new blade.

202
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:25,280
Hearteater I've named it.

203
00:17:27,740 --> 00:17:29,030
Kiss it.

204
00:17:39,130 --> 00:17:40,900
You'll kiss it again when I return

205
00:17:41,010 --> 00:17:42,990
And taste my uncle's blood.

206
00:17:42,990 --> 00:17:44,770
Will you slay him yourself?

207
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:48,130
If Stannis is fool enough to come near me.

208
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:51,380
So you'll be outside the gates fighting in the vanguard?

209
00:17:52,190 --> 00:17:56,520
A king doesn't discuss battle plans with stupid girls.

210
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:59,370
I'm sorry, Your Grace. You're right, I'm stupid.

211
00:17:59,470 --> 00:18:01,380
Of course you'll be in the vanguard.

212
00:18:02,140 --> 00:18:03,690
They say my brother Robb always goes

213
00:18:03,690 --> 00:18:05,520
where the fighting is thickest.

214
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:07,290
And he is only a pretender.

215
00:18:07,290 --> 00:18:09,130
Your brother's turn will come.

216
00:18:09,790 --> 00:18:12,930
Then you can lick his blood off Hearteater, too.

217
00:18:25,070 --> 00:18:27,960
Some of those boys will never come back.

218
00:18:28,150 --> 00:18:29,570
Joffrey will.

219
00:18:30,110 --> 00:18:31,910
The worst ones always live.

220
00:18:31,940 --> 00:18:34,820
Come, My Lady.

221
00:19:21,910 --> 00:19:25,240
- Where's our fleet? - On the way.

222
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:28,130
Why isn't it here now? They're coming.

223
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:33,240
Hound, tell the Hand that his king has asked him a question.

224
00:19:33,850 --> 00:19:36,260
The king has asked you a question.

225
00:19:36,260 --> 00:19:38,100
Ser Lancel, tell the Hound to tell the king

226
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:40,160
that the Hand is extremely busy.

227
00:19:40,170 --> 00:19:43,340
The Hand of the king would like me to tell you to tell the king...

228
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:44,990
If I tell the Hound to cut you in half,

229
00:19:44,990 --> 00:19:46,630
he'll do it without a second thought.

230
00:19:46,630 --> 00:19:48,390
That would make me the Quarterman.

231
00:19:48,410 --> 00:19:50,480
It just doesn't have the same ring to it.

232
00:19:51,730 --> 00:19:54,390
Cut me in half and I won't be able to give the signal.

233
00:19:54,630 --> 00:19:55,960
No signal, no plan.

234
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:57,370
No plan and Stannis Baratheon

235
00:19:57,370 --> 00:19:59,780
sacks this city, takes the Iron Throne,

236
00:19:59,970 --> 00:20:02,830
Puts your pinched little head atop a gate somewhere.

237
00:20:03,270 --> 00:20:04,950
It might be quite amusing,

238
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:07,220
except that my head would be up there, too.

239
00:20:07,270 --> 00:20:08,910
I've never much liked my head,

240
00:20:08,930 --> 00:20:11,630
but I don't want to see it removed just yet.

241
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:16,520
Where are their ships?

242
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:19,420
It is wise to attack at night. We took them by surprise.

243
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:22,420
Lord Varys knows what you had for breakfast three days ago.

244
00:20:22,420 --> 00:20:24,240
There are no surprises here.

245
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:26,240
If it's true there is dissention in their ranks,

246
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:28,220
maybe their sailors have mutinied.

247
00:20:28,610 --> 00:20:29,750
Maybe.

248
00:20:46,390 --> 00:20:48,140
I don't know why she wants me here.

249
00:20:48,140 --> 00:20:51,250
She's always saying how stupid I am. She hates me.

250
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:54,360
Maybe she hates you less than she hates everyone else.

251
00:20:55,470 --> 00:20:56,870
I doubt it.

252
00:20:57,410 --> 00:20:59,150
Maybe she's jealous of you.

253
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:02,130
Why would she be jealous?

254
00:21:02,250 --> 00:21:03,620
Sansa.

255
00:21:07,510 --> 00:21:10,290
I was wondering where our little dove had flown.

256
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:13,140
You look pale, child.

257
00:21:13,860 --> 00:21:15,990
Is your red flower still blooming?

258
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:17,440
Yes.

259
00:21:18,330 --> 00:21:19,800
Fitting, isn't it?

260
00:21:20,270 --> 00:21:23,250
The men will bleed out there and you will bleed in here.

261
00:21:24,250 --> 00:21:26,230
Pour Lady Sansa some wine.

262
00:21:26,230 --> 00:21:27,800
I'm not thirsty, Your Grace.

263
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:30,460
So? I didn't offer you water.

264
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:37,320
What's he doing here?

265
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:38,710
Ser Ilyn?

266
00:21:39,660 --> 00:21:41,400
He's here to defend us.

267
00:21:42,060 --> 00:21:44,070
When the axes smash down those doors,

268
00:21:44,070 --> 00:21:45,660
