541
00:43:37,460 --> 00:43:40,480
If he gets in, it will be your houses he burns,

542
00:43:41,640 --> 00:43:43,160
your gold he steals,

543
00:43:44,030 --> 00:43:45,510
your women he will rape.

544
00:43:46,650 --> 00:43:49,350
Heave! Heave!

545
00:43:49,780 --> 00:43:52,800
Heave! Heave!

546
00:43:54,910 --> 00:43:57,040
Those are brave men knocking at our door.

547
00:43:58,860 --> 00:44:00,390
Let's go kill them.

548
00:44:22,830 --> 00:44:24,440
The battle is lost, Your Grace.

549
00:44:25,640 --> 00:44:28,300
Stannis's troops are at the gates.

550
00:44:28,480 --> 00:44:30,850
When the Gold Cloaks saw the King leaving,

551
00:44:31,280 --> 00:44:33,010
they lost all heart.

552
00:44:33,400 --> 00:44:34,560
Where is my son?

553
00:44:34,930 --> 00:44:37,120
I want to escort him back to the battle.

554
00:44:37,310 --> 00:44:38,830
Why do I care what you want?

555
00:44:39,970 --> 00:44:41,560
- Bring me... - Now listen to me...

556
00:44:49,050 --> 00:44:51,970
Don't be afraid. The Queen has raised the drawbridge.

557
00:44:51,970 --> 00:44:53,990
This is the safest place we can be.

558
00:44:54,130 --> 00:44:56,620
Joffrey's not hurt. He's fighting bravely.

559
00:44:57,200 --> 00:44:59,160
His knights have rallied behind him.

560
00:44:59,160 --> 00:45:00,630
They will save the city.

561
00:45:01,540 --> 00:45:03,010
Shall we sing a hymn?

562
00:45:04,190 --> 00:45:06,450
*Gentle Mother,*

563
00:45:06,450 --> 00:45:08,670
*font of mercy,*

564
00:45:08,670 --> 00:45:13,250
*save our sons from war, we pray.*

565
00:45:13,250 --> 00:45:15,890
- *gentle... * - You must go.

566
00:45:16,310 --> 00:45:18,810
Run to your chamber and bar your door.

567
00:45:18,810 --> 00:45:21,830
Stannis won't hurt you. This one will.

568
00:45:24,620 --> 00:45:25,790
Come with me.

569
00:45:26,020 --> 00:45:27,890
I need to say goodbye to someone.

570
00:45:27,890 --> 00:45:29,830
The Queen said they'd rape everyone.

571
00:45:29,980 --> 00:45:32,040
No one is raping me.

572
00:45:34,360 --> 00:45:35,710
Go. Run.

573
00:46:14,880 --> 00:46:16,790
The lady is starting to panic.

574
00:46:18,370 --> 00:46:19,710
What are you doing here?

575
00:46:19,900 --> 00:46:21,140
Not here for long.

576
00:46:22,340 --> 00:46:24,050
- I'm going. - Where?

577
00:46:25,090 --> 00:46:27,450
Someplace that isn't burning.

578
00:46:29,730 --> 00:46:31,310
North, might be.

579
00:46:31,820 --> 00:46:32,770
Could be.

580
00:46:34,170 --> 00:46:35,350
What about the King?

581
00:46:37,040 --> 00:46:39,280
He can die just fine on his own.

582
00:46:45,550 --> 00:46:46,980
I can take you with me.

583
00:46:48,520 --> 00:46:50,110
Take you to Winterfell.

584
00:46:55,620 --> 00:46:56,960
I'll keep you safe.

585
00:46:59,910 --> 00:47:01,060
Do you want to go home?

586
00:47:05,310 --> 00:47:06,660
I'll be safe here.

587
00:47:07,360 --> 00:47:08,740
Stannis won't hurt me.

588
00:47:10,700 --> 00:47:11,710
Look at me.

589
00:47:13,640 --> 00:47:15,120
Stannis is a killer.

590
00:47:16,520 --> 00:47:18,210
The Lannisters are killers.

591
00:47:19,110 --> 00:47:20,650
Your father was a killer.

592
00:47:21,370 --> 00:47:23,630
Your brother is a killer.

593
00:47:25,210 --> 00:47:27,260
Your sons will be killers someday.

594
00:47:29,330 --> 00:47:31,480
The world is built by killers.

595
00:47:35,530 --> 00:47:37,860
So you'd better get used to looking at them.

596
00:47:41,800 --> 00:47:43,720
You won't hurt me.

597
00:47:50,520 --> 00:47:52,810
No, little bird, I won't hurt you.

598
00:48:16,030 --> 00:48:18,400
Heave! Heave!

599
00:48:24,360 --> 00:48:26,680
Come on, you bastards! Get up those ladders!

600
00:48:31,240 --> 00:48:32,250
Attack!

601
00:48:46,860 --> 00:48:48,110
Roll it over!

602
00:48:55,410 --> 00:49:00,420
Halfman! Halfman! Halfman! Halfman!

603
00:49:00,420 --> 00:49:09,420
Halfman! Halfman! Halfman! Halfman!

604
00:49:10,730 --> 00:49:12,700
Oh, fuck me.

605
00:50:06,650 --> 00:50:08,180
Be calm, my sweet.

606
00:50:08,180 --> 00:50:09,670
They're still fighting.

607
00:50:12,110 --> 00:50:13,590
No one's going to hurt you.

608
00:50:18,040 --> 00:50:19,260
I'll tell you a story.

609
00:50:21,050 --> 00:50:23,750
You know the one about the mother lion and her little cub?

610
00:50:24,250 --> 00:50:26,560
- They lived in the woods. - The Kingswood.

611
00:50:26,980 --> 00:50:28,150
Yes, my love.

612
00:50:29,070 --> 00:50:32,330
In the Kingswood there lived a mother and her cub.

613
00:50:32,840 --> 00:50:34,680
She loved him very much.

614
00:50:36,530 --> 00:50:38,420
But there were other things that lived in the woods.

615
00:50:38,420 --> 00:50:40,620
- Evil things. - Like what?

616
00:50:43,520 --> 00:50:44,950
Like stags.

617
00:50:45,870 --> 00:50:47,420
Stags aren't evil.

618
00:50:47,420 --> 00:50:49,120
They only eat grass.

619
00:50:50,110 --> 00:50:51,060
And wolves.

620
00:50:51,510 --> 00:50:52,390
My Lord.

621
00:50:53,020 --> 00:50:55,060
He could hear them howling in the night.

622
00:50:55,350 --> 00:50:57,000
The little cub was frightened.

623
00:50:57,390 --> 00:51:00,790
His mother said, "You are a lion, my son.

624
00:51:00,790 --> 00:51:02,080
You mustn't be afraid.

625
00:51:15,470 --> 00:51:17,630
For one day all the beasts will bow to you.

626
00:51:18,190 --> 00:51:19,350
You will be king.

627
00:51:22,000 --> 00:51:24,680
All the stags will bow. All the wolves will bow.

628
00:51:25,990 --> 00:51:29,230
The bears in the north and the foxes of the south,

629
00:51:30,880 --> 00:51:33,610
all the birds in the sky and the beasts in the sea--

630
00:51:36,330 --> 00:51:38,410
they will all come to you, little lion...

631
00:51:40,150 --> 00:51:42,070
to rest a crown upon your head."

632
00:51:48,120 --> 00:51:49,400
And the cub said,

633
00:51:49,520 --> 00:51:52,410
"Will I be strong and fierce like my father?"

634
00:51:53,830 --> 00:51:56,340
"Yes," Said his mother.

635
00:51:56,520 --> 00:51:59,580
"You will be strong and fierce just like your father."

636
00:52:18,080 --> 00:52:22,140
I will keep you safe, my love.

637
00:52:22,780 --> 00:52:23,890
I promise you.

638
00:52:33,240 --> 00:52:34,640
Back to the boats!

639
00:52:37,100 --> 00:52:38,460
Stand and fight!

640
00:52:40,250 --> 00:52:42,830
Stand and fight, damn you!

641
00:52:43,680 --> 00:52:45,930
No!

642
00:52:48,360 --> 00:52:49,610
Father.

643
00:52:54,770 --> 00:52:58,460
The battle is over. We have won.

644
00:53:06,970 --> 00:53:09,750
?"And who are you,"?

645
00:53:09,820 --> 00:53:11,730
?the proud lord said,?

646
00:53:11,730 --> 00:53:15,970
?"That I must bow so low?"?

647
00:53:17,340 --> 00:53:22,230
?Only a cat of a different coat?

648
00:53:22,230 --> 00:53:26,400
?that's all the truth, I know?

649
00:53:27,390 --> 00:53:32,450
?In a coat of gold or a coat of red?

650
00:53:32,450 --> 00:53:36,860
?a lion still has claws,?

651
00:53:37,380 --> 00:53:42,060
?And mine are long and sharp, My Lord,?

652
00:53:42,550 --> 00:53:46,410
?as long and sharp as yours.?

653
00:53:49,640 --> 00:53:54,270
?And so he spoke, and so he spoke,?

654
00:53:54,370 --> 00:53:59,070
?that lord of Castamere,?

655
00:54:00,080 --> 00:54:05,300
?But now the rains weep o’er his hall,?

656
00:54:05,300 --> 00:54:09,330
?with no one there to hear.?

657
00:54:09,790 --> 00:54:15,370
?Yes, now the rains weep o'er his hall,?

658
00:54:15,370 --> 00:54:20,320
?and not a soul to hear.?

